========================================================================================================
 VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  Refit speedup at the 70B geometry (L=80, m=2): 1.71x at n=64, 1.56x at n=1024.
  At L=512 (past any real stack) it reaches 36.51x -- that is where O(L^3) starts to bite.
  m=2 captures 81.6% of the dense model's held-out likelihood gain and 43.0% of the precision mass.
  Held-out NLL saturates (within 0.05 nats) at m=24 -> m=2 IS NOT sufficient on real activations.
